> Recently i came across an error (Uncaught SyntaxError: Unexpected end of JSON input at JSON.parse ) that's triggered from
> below code inside the tracer console.
> 
> 
> `    constructor(t) {
>         M(this, "_entriesPromise");
>         M(this, "_traceURL");
>         this._traceURL = t,
>         this._entriesPromise = fetch("/trace/file?path=" + encodeURIComponent(t)).then(async e=>{
>             const r = JSON.parse(await e.text())
>               , s = new Map;
>             for (const i of r.entries)
>                 s.set(i.name, i.path);
>             return s
>         }
>         `

 _Originally posted by @miordache93 in [#33328](https://github.com/microsoft/playwright/issues/33328#issuecomment-2442337912)_

This error is expected. Let's catch it and not surface it in the console.
